From 097aa797a28b806664ca2bd81d7396730752a5e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:41:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/28] feat(deploy): single-file unattended config with
 schedule provisioning

Port of the fork's 0.3.0 feature: scheduled_jobs declared in config.json
are upserted into the scheduler store at service start (Windows and
systemd), idempotently and without touching GUI-created jobs. Provisioned
jobs now go through the same validation as jobs saved from the GUI, and
an invalid one is logged and skipped.
